s recent  years  into collaboration with the veteran king  of horror the best of both worlds for  reimagining of the running man  plus this remake offers book fans a  chance to forget about the notoriously  unfaithful 1987 adaptation starring  arnold schwarzenegger  wright's already promised that he'll  stick closer to the original story  he has a deft hand with both satire and  gory violence so we're sure  that the running man can finally get the  brutal  darkly comedic cat and mouse adaptation  it deserves  in the family of stephen king  adaptations shutter's creep show series  is something like a cousin  it's the offspring of the gleefully  lurid creepshow movie which was a  collaboration between stephen king  and george romero it borrows the movie's  framework which features the titular  creep  introducing each episode's standalone  tale via the creepshow comic book but  most of its stories don't originate with  king regardless it's still part of the  family  we're always delighted to see it and  2021 will see a fresh batch of fun  spooky episodes shutter has announced a  handful of planned storylines all of  which  sound promising keith david starring in  a possible deal with the devil drama  that also  involves an exterminator sign us up  the institute may not qualify as a  classic stephen king novel in terms of  when it was published but it's still  about as  kenyan a novel as you can get kids with  special powers  sinister government agencies horror  friendship  maine and more it's fresh and new and  capable of delivering a powerful hit of  nostalgia  so it's not a surprise that someone  bought the rights immediately  a limited tv series is now in the works  with david e kelly  and jack bender working on development  this isn't their first king adaptation  they both worked on the mr mercedes tv  series something which  clearly revved them up to return to  stephen king's playground  and stephen king is a master riding what  scares us what's under our bed  so 