nue  they're set to adapt from a buick eight  a novel about a group of pennsylvania  state troopers  and the strange and dangerous car they  find themselves guarding over the years  there's no rush on the project jane said  on the podcast  the king cast that recent protests about  police brutality  make him lean towards putting such a cop  heavy story on hold but we do know that  jim mickle is attached to direct  the girl who loved tom gordon is a 1999  novel that  sort of serves as stephen king's attempt  at young adult fiction  it's a scary and gripping story about  trisha mcfarland  a lost little girl who must evade the  god of the lost  a mysterious force stalking her through  the woods she has a tiny bit of  wilderness survival knowledge and  a lot of grit and determination the  novel will be brought to the screen by  director lynn ramsey who has worked on a  wide range of interesting films that  should give her a great  toolkit for tackling the story of a girl  as tough and heroic as trisha mcfarland  fans have waited years for a film  version of the long  walk stephen king's dystopian novel  about a competition where young men  start out on a walk and can't stop or  slow down  breaking the rules gets you shot so they  must walk  or die until only one walker remains  it's a simple premise that has  nonetheless spent a long time alluding  any attempts to put it on the screen but  finally  it just might make it scary stories to  tell on the dark director  andrei overdoll has teamed up with  screenwriter james vanderbilt  known for writing the blockbuster zodiac  to attempt a successful adaptation  overdoll told comingsoon.net this script  was written on spec by james vanderbilt  when he did not even have the rights to  it he just wrote it out of pure  love for the book and in the end  suddenly the rights were open  and he was able to go to king with a  script and say  can we do this that's the kind of  devotion  we like to see and in fact newline  bought the rights so now they can  do it we can't wait until they do  carry is one of stephen king's most  adapted works  and it's set to gain yet another take as  fx has started developing a limited  series  intriguingly fx may be looking to take a  new approach to carry social isolation  collider sources suggest that it's  possible the producers will enlist  either a trans actress an actress of  color  or both to play the titular character if  so  that's an update that will let the  series say new things about how high  school society treats the people who  exist in the margins  and that's something that helps justify  this novel getting another turn in the  spotlight  hbo considers the outsider its adaption  of the stephen king thriller of the same  name to be complete after one season  a limited run series that confines  itself to the events of the novel  but that doesn't necessarily mean the  show is over there are rumors that mrc  the outsiders production company is  shopping the series around to see who  might take it up on a second season  and it's easy to see why someone would  bite the original story of the outsider  is wrapped up but stephen king's novella  if it bleeds features some of the same  characters offering material that a new  season  could easily pull from stephen king also  confirmed with entertainment weekly that  he's seen prospective season 2 scripts  it's all enough to have fans champing at  the bit for more  the third season of mr mercedes will  once again be back with viewers  even though its old home a t network  audience  is now defunct the first two seasons of  the acclaimed stephen king crime series  were previously picked up by peacock  but the third vanished with audiences  shut down however  in 2021 peacock will also acquire what  king  and director jack bender both consider  its quote  best season yet peacock has released a  short trailer for the third season  and with the first two seasons already  available for streaming  this is the perfect